你根本就没抓住精髓。
And that's the point.
That's why you're missing the point.

415
00:20:45,900 --> 00:20:48,300
我说，你可别忘了，
I mean, you're the man, remember,

416
00:20:48,340 --> 00:20:51,140
你可是连续好几年稳拿
“全英国衣着最差男人”头衔的家伙。
who has consistently,
several years running, won
Britain's Worst-Dressed Man.

417
00:20:51,180 --> 00:20:53,940
甚至还穿过工装裤配西装——
- 行了，别提那茬了！
Even in your cargo-pants suit,
- No, not now! '

418
00:20:53,980 --> 00:20:56,500
再搭上一双……
- 我现在可是上过形象改造节目的！
teamed with a...
- I've been on a makeover programme now.

419
00:20:56,540 --> 00:21:00,780
这车的高雅你根本不懂。
- 好了，稍后在节目中，
It's a car that you're just missing.
- Now, later in the programme,

420
00:21:00,820 --> 00:21:04,620
我将向大家展示我认为
有史以来最漂亮的一辆车。
I'll be showing you what I think
is the best-looking car ever.

421
00:21:04,660 --> 00:21:06,540
我不喜欢它。
- 你连是什么车都还不知道呢！
I don't like it.
- You don't know what it is!

422
00:21:06,580 --> 00:21:08,500
我不管，反正我就是不喜欢。
I don't care, I don't like it.

423
00:21:08,540 --> 00:21:10,260
几周前在我们的节目里，
Couple of weeks ago on this show,

424
00:21:10,300 --> 00:21:13,380
我们打算证明并不是所有老年人
都是马路杀手。
we set out to prove that not all old people
are dreadful drivers.

425
00:21:13,420 --> 00:21:16,540
我们邀请了几位老奶奶来上节目，
现场给我们露一手漂移画甜甜圈。
We invited grannies to come
on the show and do some doughnuts for us.

426
00:21:16,580 --> 00:21:19,100
结果报名信简直把我们淹没了。
We were inundated with responses.

427
00:21:19,140 --> 00:21:22,380
于是我们选出了这五位
可爱的老太太来大显身手。
So we picked these five
lovely ladies to have a go.

428
00:21:22,420 --> 00:21:26,500
哈蒙德：欢迎来到《Top Gear》
老奶奶甜甜圈挑战赛！
HAMMOND: Welcome to the Top Gear
Granny Doughnut Challenge.

429
00:21:26,540 --> 00:21:29,860
如大家所见，老奶奶们已经就位了，而她们要开的车，
These are the grannies
as you know, and the car they'll be driving

430
00:21:29,900 --> 00:21:33,500
是一辆运动型后驱跑车——本田S2000。
is a sporty rear-wheel drive Honda S2000.

431
00:21:33,540 --> 00:21:35,540
噢，太俊了！
- 您喜欢吗？
Oh, it's gorgeous.
- You like it?

432
00:21:35,580 --> 00:21:36,900
棒极了，我太喜欢了。
It's fantastic. Yes, I do.

433
00:21:36,940 --> 00:21:40,260
您打算坐后排吗？
- 才不呢！
[笑声]
Are you going in the back?
- No!
[LAUGHTER]

434
00:21:40,300 --> 00:21:44,460
让我儿子坐后排去！
My son is going in the back!

435
00:21:44,500 --> 00:21:48,140
哈蒙德：但在画甜甜圈之前，
先是吃蛋糕的时间。
HAMMOND: But before the doughnuts,
it was cake time.

436
00:21:48,180 --> 00:21:51,420
铺上一层面皮，
均匀抹上一层猪油，
You put your layers,
you spread it over with lard,

437
00:21:51,460 --> 00:21:56,780
然后一层层铺上
什锦果干、肉桂粉和白糖。
and then put your layers
of mixed fruit and cinnamon and sugar in.

438
00:21:56,820 --> 00:22:00,980
要是去妇女联合会的集市，
买吃的可一定要去那儿，
因为全都是纯手工自制的。
If you go in the WI market, you
want to get your food there,
because that's all home-made.

439
00:22:01,020 --> 00:22:02,860
在那儿能买到我的黑莓果酱吗？
- 当然可以。
Can I get my bramble jelly there?
- You can.

440
00:22:02,900 --> 00:22:05,340
可以的。
- 肯定能买到。
You can.
- Should be able to.

441
00:22:05,380 --> 00:22:09,700
哈蒙德：负责给老太太们授课的，
是王牌特技车手拉斯·斯威夫特。
HAMMOND:  The man who'll be teaching them
is ace stunt driver Russ Swift.

442
00:22:09,740 --> 00:22:11,700
这里的要领是，
车速一定要放得很慢。
The idea is you want to
approach it fairly slowly.

443
00:22:11,740 --> 00:22:13,460
这套动作根本不需要快开。
It's not a very fast manoeuvre at all.

444
00:22:13,500 --> 00:22:17,540
挂上一档，然后打方向，
就像要原地画圈一样，
First gear, and then you're going to turn
as if going in a circle,

445
00:22:17,580 --> 00:22:21,340
接着踩下离合，把转速轰上去，
让后轮疯狂烧胎打滑。
and then you'll probably dip the clutch,
build the revs up and spin the back wheels.

446
00:22:21,380 --> 00:22:23,860
然后就会看到……
And what'll happen then...

447
00:22:23,900 --> 00:22:27,860
哈蒙德：显然，黑板上的粉笔字
根本无法替代清晨烧焦的橡胶味——
HAMMOND: Obviously, chalk on
a blackboard is no substitute
for the smell of burning rubber

448
00:22:27,900 --> 00:22:30,220
正如拉斯所演示的这样。
in the morning, as Russ demonstrates.

449
00:22:31,380 --> 00:22:34,660
[轮胎尖叫声]
[TYRES SCREECH]

450
00:22:38,140 --> 00:22:40,500
噢！
Ooh!

451
00:22:40,540 --> 00:22:44,460
他的前轮都快……
[大笑]
His front wheels are almost...
[LAUGHING]

452
00:22:44,500 --> 00:22:47,660
小菜一碟。
- 再来一次，看他还能不能再成一次。
Easy-peasy.
- Do it again. See if he can do it again.

453
00:22:50,620 --> 00:22:55,260
你带成人纸尿裤了吗？！
- 没，我没带。
Did you bring your incontinence pads!?
- No, I didn't.

454
00:22:55,300 --> 00:22:58,060
行了。现在我们见识过标准操作了，对吧？
All right. Now, we've seen
how you're meant to do it, OK?

455
00:22:58,100 --> 00:23:01,820
稍后我们再瞧瞧老太太们学得怎么样。
We'll find out how they got on, later on.

456
00:23:01,860 --> 00:23:06,660
我已经迫不及待想看老奶奶们上手了，真等不及了。
I can't wait to see those grannies
trying that. I just can't wait.

457
00:23:06,700 --> 00:23:08,660
但我们不得不先等等，因为……
But we're going to have to, because

458
00:23:08,700 --> 00:23:11,380
每周我们都会请来一位明星嘉宾。
every week we have a celebrity guest.

459
00:23:11,420 --> 00:23:13,300
现在有请这位大腕，
And now it's time to meet him,

460
00:23:13,340 --> 00:23:17,380
他是《终极特警》的主演，
还演过一部叫《东区人》的玩意儿。
he is the star of Ultimate Force and also
of something called EastEnders.

461
00:23:17,420 --> 00:23:19,980
女士们先生们，罗斯·坎普！
Ladies and gentlemen, Ross Kemp!

462
00:23:20,020 --> 00:23:24,100
[掌声]
[APPLAUSE]

463
00:23:24,140 --> 00:23:27,540
最近怎么样？还行吧？
- 挺好的。请坐。
How are you? All right?
- Very well. Have a seat.

464
00:23:30,460 --> 00:23:34,220
你奶奶能玩出这手吗？
[笑声]
Could your granny do that?
[LAUGHS]

465
00:23:34,260 --> 00:23:36,260
我奶奶都86岁了！
My granny's 86!

466
00:23:36,300 --> 00:23:40,300
她早就不玩原地甩尾了，
不过苹果派倒是烤得一绝。
She doesn't really do doughnuts anymore.
She makes nice apple pies.

467
00:23:40,340 --> 00:23:42,460
你自己试过甩尾甜甜圈吗？
Have you ever tried one?

468
00:23:42,500 --> 00:23:45,860
试过，没成功，我不太擅长玩这种花活。
Yes, unsuccessfully, I'm not that good
at doing things like that.

469
00:23:45,900 --> 00:23:47,740
戏里的特技驾驶全是你亲自上的，对吧？
You do all your own
stunt driving, don't you?

470
00:23:47,780 --> 00:23:50,860
这话有点夸大了。不是全部，但大部分都是我亲自开的。
That is a misnomer. I don't do all my
stunt driving. I do a lot of it.

471
00:23:50,900 --> 00:23:52,980
特别是在拍《东区人》那会儿。
Especially when we were in EastEnders.

472
00:23:53,020 --> 00:23:57,140
跟我一起搭戏的哥们儿都能作证，
我可没在……
You know, the guys
I worked with can testify that I'm not...

473
00:23:57,180 --> 00:23:58,500
满嘴跑火车。
telling porkie pies now.

474
00:23:58,540 --> 00:24:00,420
绝大多数都是我亲自来的。
- 他们人呢？
I did most of it.
- Who are they?

475
00:24:00,460 --> 00:24:02,580
就在那边。兄弟们，挥个手！
Over there. Wave, boys.

476
00:24:02,620 --> 00:24:05,940
特技真是他自己开的吗？
- 罗伯！
Did he do his stunts?
- Rob!

477
00:24:05,980 --> 00:24:07,740
“真是他”。
非常感谢！待会儿见。
"He did".
Thank you very much. I'll see you later.

478
00:24:07,780 --> 00:24:10,260
你平时开什么车？来，让我……
What do you drive? Go on. Let me...

479
00:24:10,300 --> 00:24:11,980
其实我还真猜不出来。
I can't guess, actually.

480
00:24:12,020 --> 00:24:13,500
我开一辆 996 Turbo。
I drive a 996 Turbo.

481
00:24:13,540 --> 00:24:14,980
噢，911？
- 没错。
Oh, a 911?
- Yeah.

482
00:24:15,020 --> 00:24:16,980
这车挺不错的。
- 是相当不错。
It's quite a nice car.
- It's a very nice car.

483
00:24:17,020 --> 00:24:19,500
确实不错。我真不想承认这点，
Actually, it is. I hate to say this

484
00:24:19,540 --> 00:24:21,940
因为我向来讨厌911。
'cause I've always hated 911s.

485
00:24:21,980 --> 00:24:24,820
为什么？
- 发动机装错位置了。
Why?
- The engine is in the wrong place.

486
00:24:24,860 --> 00:24:27,580
那应该装哪儿？驾驶员坐的地方？后头？不是吧……
Where should it be then? Where the
driver is, at the back? No...

487
00:24:27,620 --> 00:24:29,460
不是……
- 它是装在车身中部的。
No...
- It's in the middle of the car.

488
00:24:29,500 --> 00:24:34,540
以前的911是在后头。
但现在的发动机是放在正中间，
911, it was in the back.
But now it sits in the centre of the car,

489
00:24:34,580 --> 00:24:36,100
也就是F1赛车放发动机的位置。
which is where the Formula One engine is.

490
00:24:36,140 --> 00:24:38,300
它依然是后置发动机的好吗。
It's a rear-engine car, still.

491
00:24:38,340 --> 00:24:42,060
即便到了现在，它也是后置。
大家说我说得对不对？
Even now, it is a rear engine.
Am I right?

492
00:24:42,100 --> 00:24:43,460
观众：对！
- 才不是。
AUDIENCE: Yeah.
- No.

493
00:24:44,700 --> 00:24:47,340
现场这帮全都是车呆子。
They're all car bores here.

494
00:24:47,380 --> 00:24:51,660
上周咱们聊到一个事儿，我说，
We had a thing last week where I said,

495
00:24:51,700 --> 00:24:53,980
“电视机前的观众朋友们，
"Would you, to any
of the people watching at home

496
00:24:54,020 --> 00:24:57,180
谁想来提名身边哪个你觉得是‘车呆子’的人？”
like to nominate someone
who you think is a car bore?"

497
00:24:57,220 --> 00:25:00,740
我们本以为顶多收到六七封回复。
We thought we'd get six or seven replies.

498
00:25:00,780 --> 00:25:04,620
你们知道有多少人写信说
“我正和一个车呆子同居”吗？
Do you know how many people
wrote in and said,
"I am living with a car bore"?

499
00:25:04,660 --> 00:25:08,420
一千五百封。清一色全是女人！
1,500. All women!

500
00:25:08,460 --> 00:25:09,900
一个例外都没有。
Every single one of them.

501
00:25:09,940 --> 00:25:11,620
其中一位写道，
One of them said,

502
00:25:11,660 --> 00:25:15,500
“我男朋友每晚躺在床上都要看海恩斯维修手册。”
"My boyfriend
reads a Haynes manual in bed every night."

503
00:25:16,420 --> 00:25:18,900
看的还是他根本就没买的车！
For a car he doesn't own!

504
00:25:22,020 --> 00:25:23,460
我也想玩这个游戏了。
I want to play this game.

505
00:25:23,500 --> 00:25:25,580
上周杰·凯来上节目时我们就玩过。
We played it with Jay Kay
who came on the show last week.

506
00:25:25,620 --> 00:25:27,620
他猜这玩意儿简直厉害得吓人。
He was frighteningly good at it.

507
00:25:27,660 --> 00:25:29,140
规则就是，一开始只给看一小块细节，
You know, you start off
with a little something

508
00:25:29,180 --> 00:25:31,180
然后看看我们能不能猜出来。我完全没头绪。
and we'll see if we can guess.
I have no clue.

509
00:25:31,220 --> 00:25:33,340
现场观众们，随时欢迎你们一起猜。
Audience, you're more than
welcome to join in.

510
00:25:33,380 --> 00:25:35,820
放第一张图吧。
看看能不能猜出是什么。
Let's bring the first one up.
See if we can guess what it is.

511
00:25:38,100 --> 00:25:39,420
那是……
That's a...

512
00:25:39,460 --> 00:25:41,020
什么？
男观众：奥迪TT！
What?
MAN: An Audi TT.

513
00:25:41,060 --> 00:25:44,540
奥迪TT？让我们瞧瞧。
镜头拉远一点。
An Audi TT? Let's have a look.
Pull it out a bit.

514
00:25:44,580 --> 00:25:47,020
还真是，真是一辆TT。
- 一眼就能看出来。
It is, it's a TT.
- As you can tell.

515
00:25:47,060 --> 00:25:49,140
你们这帮人真可悲！
You are pathetic!

516
00:25:50,140 --> 00:25:52,780
[掌声]
[APPLAUSE]

517
00:25:54,900 --> 00:25:58,540
好吧，咱们俩被狠狠打脸了。
看下一个。
Well, both of us got blasted there.
Let's have the next one.

518
00:25:58,580 --> 00:26:00,340
噢，我估摸着我知道这是什么了。
Oh, I know what that is I reckon.

519
00:26:00,380 --> 00:26:02,380
你想碰碰运气猜一下吗？
- 毫无头绪。
Do you want to hazard a guess?
- Not a clue.

520
00:26:02,420 --> 00:26:05,740
只有一家车厂到现在还把铰链露在外面。
One only car firm still puts its hinges
on the outside.

521
00:26:05,780 --> 00:26:07,820
我连这是哪家车厂都认不出。
I don't even know which car firm that is.

522
00:26:07,860 --> 00:26:09,900
索利哈尔造的吧，我猜。
Solihull, I reckon.

523
00:26:09,940 --> 00:26:13,460
我来瞎蒙一个。
路虎。
I am going to have a stab at this one.
Land Rover.

524
00:26:13,500 --> 00:26:16,780
一辆卫士。镜头拉远点。
- 答对了。
A Defender. Go out.
- You're right.

525
00:26:16,820 --> 00:26:18,500
感觉来了。
- 你说得对。
Feeling confident.
- You're right.

526
00:26:18,540 --> 00:26:20,860
噢，我猜中一个！
Ooh, I've got one!

527
00:26:20,900 --> 00:26:23,420
这可是我两周以来头一次蒙对。
That's the first one I've had in two weeks.

528
00:26:23,460 --> 00:26:26,780
全貌出来了。漂亮，这道不错。
来看看下一张。
There it is. Good one, that one. Let's have
a look at the next one.

529
00:26:26,820 --> 00:26:28,660
坎普：卡利布拉……？
KEMP: Calibra...?

530
00:26:28,700 --> 00:26:31,980
克拉克森：轮廓像卡利布拉，
但这大灯看着太现代了。
CLARKSON: Calibra shape, but
the headlamps are too modern for it.

531
00:26:32,020 --> 00:26:34,300
呃……
Um.

532
00:26:34,340 --> 00:26:37,380
有人知道吗？快点。
- 赶紧的。
Anyone? Come on.
- C'mon.

533
00:26:37,420 --> 00:26:40,300
观众男：阿尔法·罗密欧？
- 阿尔法·罗密欧哪款？
MAN: Alfa Romeo?
- Alfa Romeo what?

534
00:26:40,340 --> 00:26:42,700
观众男：朋多。
- 是朋多。
MAN: Punto.
- It's a Punto.

535
00:26:42,740 --> 00:26:44,740
你怎么看出来的？你压根都看不清！
How do you know? You can't even see!

536
00:26:44,780 --> 00:26:48,860
我看现场这帮人全都是学汽车设计的吧。
All these people are doing courses
in designing cars, I believe.

537
00:26:48,900 --> 00:26:52,780
[结巴] 要那是辆朋多……
搞不好其实是辆西雅特。
[STUTTERS] If that's a Punto...
it could be a Seat actually.

538
00:26:52,820 --> 00:26:55,900
不，绝对不是。肯定是朋多。
No, it's not. It's gonna be a Punto.

539
00:26:55,940 --> 00:26:59,860
你有女朋友吗？
[笑声]
Do you have a girlfriend?
[LAUGHTER]

540
00:26:59,900 --> 00:27:03,020
你平时也跟女朋友聊这种玩意儿？
Do you talk to your girlfriend
about that sort of thing?

541
00:27:03,060 --> 00:27:07,940
走在大街上你是不是也这样，
对着街边嚷嚷：“看，那是……”
You walk down the street
like this going, "That's a..."

542
00:27:07,980 --> 00:27:11,300
“那是一辆希尔曼猎人。”
行了，换下一张。
"It's a Hillman Hunter."
Come on. Let's bring up another one.

543
00:27:11,340 --> 00:27:12,700
好嘞，看这辆。
OK. Here we go.

544
00:27:12,740 --> 00:27:15,380
这是博克斯特吧？
That's a Boxster, isn't it?

545
00:27:15,420 --> 00:27:18,340
是博克斯特吗？
- 也可能是辆Turbo。
Is it a Boxster?
- Or it could be a turbo.

546
00:27:18,380 --> 00:27:22,940
瞧瞧看，镜头拉远。
看看罗斯……
- Turbo。
Let's have a look. Pull out.
Let's see if Ross...
- Turbo.

547
00:27:22,980 --> 00:27:24,340
是不是……
Is it a...

548
00:27:25,660 --> 00:27:27,540
这就是你自己的车！
- 还真是我那辆。
It's your car!
- It is my car.

549
00:27:28,820 --> 00:27:30,900
怪不得我能认出来！
- 干得漂亮，罗斯。
That's why I got that one!
- Well done, Ross.

550
00:27:32,780 --> 00:27:35,780
你那辆911，平时可不止是开着买菜遛弯吧。
