00:33:23,900 --> 00:33:27,220
克拉克森：阿斯顿·马丁推出了DB7。
（那是1994年）
CLARKSON: Aston Martin launched the DB7.
(In 1994)

683
00:33:37,740 --> 00:33:40,580
噢，这动静可真迷人。
Ooh. That's a lovely noise.

684
00:33:40,620 --> 00:33:43,620
但说老实话，
我能把这车喷得体无完肤。
But to be honest,
I could pull this car apart.

685
00:33:43,660 --> 00:33:46,020
早期车型的做工烂得一塌糊涂，
The early models were very badly made,

686
00:33:46,060 --> 00:33:48,140
而且毛病还不止一两处。
and it wasn't just one thing, either.

687
00:33:48,180 --> 00:33:50,980
有些自燃了，
有些直接半路趴窝。
Some of them caught fire,
some of them just stopped.

688
00:33:51,020 --> 00:33:54,340
我自己开过的那台，拼装得
就跟“薯头先生”积木玩具似的。
The one I had, had been built
like Mr Potato Head.

689
00:33:54,380 --> 00:33:57,260
开着开着就散架了。
It just sort of fell apart.

690
00:33:57,300 --> 00:34:00,980
还不止这些呢，
它是基于捷豹XJS底盘造出来的，
There's more too,
it's based on the Jaguar XJS,

691
00:34:01,020 --> 00:34:04,140
这意味着它的底子
到现在已经有25年历史了。
which means its underpinnings
are 25 years old now.

692
00:34:04,180 --> 00:34:07,740
要按狗的年龄折算，它都438岁了。
And in dog years, that makes it 438.

693
00:34:10,660 --> 00:34:12,540
自动恒温空调呢？
Where's the climate control?

694
00:34:12,580 --> 00:34:14,980
雷达自适应巡航呢？
Where's the radar-guided cruise control?

695
00:34:15,020 --> 00:34:18,580
车上装的这些设备，
语音控制又上哪儿去了？
Where's the voice activation
for all the equipment you do get?

696
00:34:18,620 --> 00:34:22,940
英国广播二台。播放CD第三首。
Radio Two. CD track three.

697
00:34:22,980 --> 00:34:24,980
屁反应没有。
Nothing.

698
00:34:25,020 --> 00:34:27,780
现在这些配置，你花一半价钱
买辆捷豹都能全配齐。
You can get that sort of stuff
these days on a Jag costing half the price.

699
00:34:27,820 --> 00:34:29,780
但在这车上？门儿都没有。
But not in this.

700
00:34:30,460 --> 00:34:32,260
[发动机轰鸣]
[ENGINE REVS]

701
00:34:34,700 --> 00:34:36,580
明白我说那声浪是啥意思了吧？
See what I mean about the noise?

702
00:34:36,620 --> 00:34:38,620
但这冲劲儿哪去了？
But where's the get-up-and-go?

703
00:34:38,660 --> 00:34:43,460
哪怕装了一台6.0升V12发动机，它的威力
还没个街道居委会大。
Even with a six-litre V12, it's no more
powerful than a parish council.

704
00:34:45,060 --> 00:34:47,980
我还想问呢，头部空间去哪了？
I might also ask, where's the headroom?

705
00:34:48,020 --> 00:34:51,740
瞧瞧，问题在于发动机电脑
就塞在驾驶座正下方。
See, the problem is, the engine's computer
is underneath the driver's seat.

706
00:34:51,780 --> 00:34:54,180
搞得你坐上去
感觉像坐在婴儿高脚椅上。
So it feels like
you're sitting on a highchair.

707
00:34:54,220 --> 00:34:58,780
敞篷版就更遭罪了，
因为车顶差不多就在这儿。
And it's even worse in the convertible.
'Cause the roof's about here.

708
00:35:01,260 --> 00:35:02,940
我能在这儿叨叨一整天，
I could go on all day,

709
00:35:02,980 --> 00:35:05,460
数落这辆车浑身上下的毛病。
listing things that are wrong
with this car.

710
00:35:05,500 --> 00:35:07,260
但你琢磨琢磨，
But think about it,

711
00:35:07,300 --> 00:35:09,420
要是你真有一台，晚上准备出门潇洒，
if you had one, and you were going out
in the evening,

712
00:35:09,460 --> 00:35:13,100
你就可以说：“今晚咱开阿斯顿去？”
you could say, "Shall we take the Aston?"

713
00:35:13,140 --> 00:35:15,260
这听起来可太有面子了，不是吗？
And that sounds pretty good, doesn't it?

714
00:35:16,780 --> 00:35:17,860
倍儿有面子。
Pretty good.

715
00:35:19,060 --> 00:35:21,020
“今晚咱开阿斯顿去？”
Shall we take the Aston?

716
00:35:21,060 --> 00:35:22,420
阿斯顿。
Aston.

717
00:35:22,440 --> 00:35:25,440
♪ 约翰·帕赫贝尔 - 《D大调卡农》 ♪
♪ Johann Pachelbel - Canon in D ♪

718
00:35:27,940 --> 00:35:32,380
当你漫游在梅费尔区，
掠过珀迪猎枪店、蒂芙尼和克拉里奇酒店，
As you cruise round Mayfair,
past Purdy, and Tiffany and Claridges,

719
00:35:32,420 --> 00:35:34,580
开着这种车，你会感觉自己完全属于这里。
you feel at home in a car like this.

720
00:35:34,620 --> 00:35:36,060
而且这绝不仅仅是因为它的名头
And it's not just the name

721
00:35:36,100 --> 00:35:38,300
直让人浑身起鸡皮疙瘩。
that sends a shiver down the spine.

722
00:35:38,340 --> 00:35:40,220
全凭这张盛世美颜。
It's the looks.

723
00:35:57,020 --> 00:36:01,780
而且我觉得，甚至不能只用
“在车里算好看”来形容DB7。
And I don't think the DB7
is good-looking for a car, either.

724
00:36:01,820 --> 00:36:05,300
在我眼里，人类有史以来
造出过的三样最美之物是：
For me, the three best-looking things
ever made by man are,

725
00:36:05,340 --> 00:36:08,220
排在第三的，
亨伯悬索桥；
at number three,
the Humber Suspension Bridge,

726
00:36:08,260 --> 00:36:14,340
排在第二的，SR-71侦察机；
而高居榜首的，就是它——
at number two, the SR71 spy plane,
and at number one, this,

727
00:36:16,380 --> 00:36:19,180
阿斯顿·马丁 DB7。
the Aston Martin DB7.

728
00:36:37,780 --> 00:36:40,660
每当迈克尔·帕金森
在节目里请来板球明星，
When Michael Parkinson
has a cricketer on his show,

729
00:36:40,700 --> 00:36:43,740
你就会听到那种调调……
【模仿帕金森】我下一位嘉宾
堪称旷世奇才，
and you get that...
[AS PARKINSON] My next guest
is a remarkable man,

730
00:36:43,780 --> 00:36:46,580
物理定律在他面前形同虚设，
the laws of physics mean nothing to him,

731
00:36:46,620 --> 00:36:49,020
老夫但凡长了卵巢，
都恨不得给他生孩子。
and if I had ovaries,
I'd bear his children.

732
00:36:49,060 --> 00:36:51,500
【正常声音】
好吧，我现在差不多也是这感觉。因为——
[NORMAL VOICE]
Well, that's how I feel right now. Because

733
00:36:51,540 --> 00:36:55,020
今天坐在我身边的，正是操刀
设计出DB7的大师，伊恩·卡勒姆。
I'm joined by the man
who designed the DB7, Ian Callum.

734
00:36:55,060 --> 00:36:58,380
我说伊恩，你知道伊凡雷帝吧？
Now, Ian. You know Ivan the Terrible?

735
00:36:58,420 --> 00:37:00,060
你肯定不认识他。
但当年伊凡雷帝……
You don't know him.
But Ivan the Terrible...

736
00:37:00,100 --> 00:37:04,420
当手下在圣彼得堡建好大教堂后，
When his people had built
the Basilica in St Petersburg,

737
00:37:04,460 --> 00:37:06,940
他下令挖掉了工匠们的眼珠子，
he had their eyes gouged out

738
00:37:06,980 --> 00:37:09,620
免得他们以后再造出更好的作品。
- 嗯哼。
so that they'd never do anything better.
- Mm-hm.

739
00:37:09,660 --> 00:37:14,700
阿斯顿·马丁当年有人对你说过：
“伊恩，老兄，我们得挖了你的眼珠子，
Did anyone at Aston Martin say,
"Ian, we've got to have your eyes, mate?

740
00:37:14,740 --> 00:37:17,060
“因为你这辈子再也无法超越它了”吗？
"'Cause you'll never top this."

741
00:37:17,100 --> 00:37:19,180
尤其是你如果跳槽去别家的话。你现在在哪高就？
Certainly not if you go to work for
someone else. Where are you now?

742
00:37:19,220 --> 00:37:21,420
我现在在捷豹。
- 没错。
I am at Jaguar.
- Yeah.

743
00:37:21,460 --> 00:37:24,500
他们得先把Vanquish要走，
所以之前还照应了我一阵子。
They wanted the Vanquish first.
So they looked after me for a little while.

744
00:37:24,540 --> 00:37:27,500
那又是个尤物，
绝对的人间尤物。
- 确实还算过得去。
That's another beauty.
That's an absolute beauty.
- It's not bad.

745
00:37:27,540 --> 00:37:31,220
各位，你们知道
真正恐怖的是什么吗？
And do you know
the really scary thing, everybody?

746
00:37:31,260 --> 00:37:35,340
我听说我们以后
再也见不到这种车了，
I've heard we'll never see
the like of cars this ever again,

747
00:37:35,380 --> 00:37:38,380
全拜……法规所赐。
because of... legislation.

748
00:37:38,420 --> 00:37:40,420
法规。
- 布鲁塞尔搞出来的？
Legislation.
- From Brussels?

749
00:37:40,460 --> 00:37:44,060
倒也不全是。还有汽车行业内部的，
属于行业自律规范。
Not necessarily. It's also from the
car industry itself. It's self-policing.

750
00:37:44,100 --> 00:37:46,580
是吗？
- 是行人保护法规。
Is it?
- It's pedestrian legislation.

751
00:37:46,620 --> 00:37:51,340
要是过几年再让你设计DB7，
会有哪些东西被彻底禁止？
What kind of things wouldn't be allowed
if you did the DB7 in a few years' time?

752
00:37:51,380 --> 00:37:53,500
到底会有什么大变样？
What is it that's going to change?

753
00:37:53,540 --> 00:37:55,300
行人保护法规硬性规定，
Pedestrian legislation dictates

754
00:37:55,340 --> 00:37:58,020
引擎盖和发动机之间必须留出大片缓冲间隙。
you have to have a lot of air
between the bonnet and the engine.

755
00:37:58,060 --> 00:38:02,700
这样万一把人给撞了，
他们的脑袋砸在引擎盖上……
- 机盖能凹陷变形吸收冲击。
So if you run someone over,
their head hits the bonnet...
- Can deform into the bonnet.

756
00:38:02,740 --> 00:38:04,540
要留多大的空隙？
- 大概三英寸。
How much air?
- About three inches.

757
00:38:04,580 --> 00:38:06,580
所以你就得把机盖……
- 必须得隆起。
So you're gonna need to get that bonnet...
- Absolutely.

758
00:38:06,620 --> 00:38:10,740
就没法压得那么低平优美了。
- 我们不得不把它垫高到发动机上方。
You can't smooth it over.
- We've got to lift it above the engine.

759
00:38:10,780 --> 00:38:12,620
不过，新技术或许能救个场。
However, technology might help us there.

760
00:38:12,660 --> 00:38:15,260
我们也许可以做主动弹起式引擎盖。
但这玩意儿难度极高……
We may be able to deploy the bonnet.
That's a very difficult thing...

761
00:38:15,300 --> 00:38:18,020
弹出？
- 引擎盖真的会弹起来，没错。
Deploy it?
- Actually deploy the bonnet. Yes.

762
00:38:18,060 --> 00:38:20,220
什么叫“弹出来”？
- 它真的会往上顶起来。
What do you mean, deploy it?
- It actually lifts up.

763
00:38:20,260 --> 00:38:21,940
撞到人的时候？
- 对。
When you hit someone?
- Yes.

764
00:38:21,980 --> 00:38:23,980
太棒了！
- 这技术难度其实极大。
Fantastic!
- It's very difficult.

765
00:38:24,020 --> 00:38:25,420
[众人七嘴八舌]
[OVERLAPPING CHATTER]

766
00:38:25,460 --> 00:38:28,180
“我要撞那个人了，
快看我的引擎盖！”
I'm gonna run that person over.
Look at my bonnet!

767
00:38:30,660 --> 00:38:32,260
你觉得这有可能实现吗？
You think, that might be possible?

768
00:38:32,300 --> 00:38:34,740
也许可行，
但不是眼下的解决办法。
That may be possible,
but it's not the immediate answer.

769
00:38:34,780 --> 00:38:38,100
而且还有其他法规马上要出台，
There's also other legislation coming in,

770
00:38:38,140 --> 00:38:42,540
主要是美国那边的，
要求保护不系安全带的乘员。
mainly from the US,
for looking after unbelted occupants.

771
00:38:42,580 --> 00:38:47,300
也就是那些开车
还不系安全带的人。
我们还得负责照顾他们。
That's people who drive a car
who do not wear seatbelts.
We must look after them.

772
00:38:47,340 --> 00:38:49,540
按法律规定是这样。
According to the law.

773
00:38:49,580 --> 00:38:51,420
美国的法律？
- 千真万确。
American law?
- Absolutely.

774
00:38:51,460 --> 00:38:53,020
要是他们不……
- 很多美国人……
If they don't...
- Many Americans...

775
00:38:53,060 --> 00:38:56,780
（模仿美国口音）我太胖了……
- ……都不系安全带。
IN AMERICAN ACCENT: I'm too fat...
- ...don't wear seatbelts.

776
00:38:56,820 --> 00:38:58,540
真的假的？
- 真的，绝对是这样。
Really?
- Really. Absolutely.

777
00:38:58,580 --> 00:39:00,260
而你们还得保护他们？
- 我们还得保护他们。
And you have to protect them?
- And we have to protect them.

778
00:39:00,300 --> 00:39:02,740
免得他们把自己伤着。
- 没错。
So that they don't hurt themselves.
- Absolutely.

779
00:39:02,780 --> 00:39:05,660
那这会让车头造型
发生什么变化？
How will this change the shape
of the front?

780
00:39:05,700 --> 00:39:09,420
嗯，实际情况是，
我们会计算头部的运动轨迹，
Well, what happens is
we calculate the trajectory of the head,

781
00:39:09,460 --> 00:39:13,940
进而确定从车头这里
延伸进去的一套结构空间包络。
and that sets up a package which comes in
through the front of the car here.

782
00:39:13,980 --> 00:39:18,780
这里的这个点必须往上提，
可能还得往前移，
This point here has to go up
and possibly forwards,

783
00:39:18,820 --> 00:39:20,660
这就意味着
挡风玻璃可能会拉得更深。
which means
the screen probably gets deeper.

784
00:39:20,700 --> 00:39:21,860
因为……
- 你不能假定……
Because...
- You can't presume...

785
00:39:21,900 --> 00:39:23,860
你得把那块往外挪。
- 没错。
You'll have to move that out.
- Yes.

786
00:39:23,900 --> 00:39:26,860
所以那块会凸出来。
那不就成《邮递员派特》的面包车了嘛！
So, that will come out.
That's Postman Pat's van!

787
00:39:28,660 --> 00:39:30,860
要是从这里一直拉平过去……
If you've got it to here
and straight along...

788
00:39:30,900 --> 00:39:35,060
这么说可能夸张了点，
不过我们在单位确实管它叫冰淇淋车。
That's probably exaggerating but we do
call it the ice cream van, at work.

789
00:39:35,100 --> 00:39:37,420
听着，我现在想干件事，行吗？
- 行啊。
I'll tell you what I'd like to do now, OK?
- Yes.

790
00:39:37,460 --> 00:39:39,540
那就是……我特别喜欢看
Is... I love it

791
00:39:39,580 --> 00:39:41,460
这些汽车设计师，
when I see these car designers,

792
00:39:41,500 --> 00:39:45,140
只要给他们纸和笔，
就能把车画得神乎其神。
they can draw cars beautifully
when you just give them a pen and paper.

793
00:39:45,180 --> 00:39:47,260
有些人确实画得好。
- 得了吧你！
Some of them can.
- Don't!

794
00:39:47,300 --> 00:39:51,060
你要是能设计出 Escort Cosworth 之类的，你就肯定会画。
（是弗兰克·斯蒂芬森设计的？）
If you did the Escort Cosworth
and that, you can draw.
(Frank Stephenson?)

795
00:39:51,100 --> 00:39:54,420
把彼得也叫过来。
这是你的画架。
Let's get Peter in as well.
This is your easel here.

796
00:39:54,460 --> 00:39:56,300
伊恩，那是你的画架。
Ian, that's your easel there.

797
00:39:56,340 --> 00:39:58,940
咱们得想想让他们画点什么。大家有什么建议吗？
We want to think of something
we want them to draw. Any suggestions?

798
00:39:58,980 --> 00:40:03,300
男观众：翼豹（Impreza）！
- 来点咱们未来想见到的车。
MAN: Impreza.
- Something we want to see in the future.

799
00:40:03,340 --> 00:40:07,220
男观众2：E-Type！
- E-Type。
MAN 2: E-Type.
- E-Type.

800
00:40:07,260 --> 00:40:10,100
画一辆现代版的 E-Type 怎么样？
How about a modern day E-Type?

801
00:40:10,140 --> 00:40:12,420
既然你在捷豹工作，
这应该难不倒你。
Since you're at Jaguar,
this shouldn't be too difficult.

802
00:40:12,460 --> 00:40:15,620
你也在捷豹，只不过职位更高。
You're at Jaguar as well, but higher up.

803
00:40:15,660 --> 00:40:18,900
二位现在可以开工了。
You can both get cracking, now.

804
00:40:19,820 --> 00:40:21,860
我说，不如这样。
I tell you what.

805
00:40:21,900 --> 00:40:25,940
这儿还有个画架，我也来露一手。
Another easel here. I'll have a go as well.

806
00:40:25,980 --> 00:40:28,540
当个汽车设计师能有多难？
（史上第一次出现“能有多难”）
How hard can it be to be a car designer?
(First ever 'how hard can it be')

807
00:40:30,140 --> 00:40:33,860
彼得，你用这个画架没问题吧？
毕竟你在沃尔沃干过，
Peter, is this okay for you,
because having worked at Volvo,

808
00:40:33,900 --> 00:40:35,420
他们以前可都用画方块的神奇画板。
they had Etch-A-Sketches.

809
00:40:35,460 --> 00:40:37,820
确实如此，我们不用电脑。
That's true. We don't use computers.

810
00:40:39,660 --> 00:40:43,820
我先从车轮画起。
有人带硬币能借我描个圆圈吗？
I'm gonna start with the wheels.
Anyone got a coin I can draw around?

811
00:40:43,860 --> 00:40:46,820
你们画的时候会考虑现行法规，
Are you gonna be doing it
with current legislation in mind,

812
00:40:46,860 --> 00:40:50,060
还是抛开美国人的指手画脚，
or are you going to be doing what you'd
like to do without the Americans

813
00:40:50,100 --> 00:40:51,420
想怎么画就怎么画？
being involved?

814
00:40:51,460 --> 00:40:54,420
伊恩：画我们真正想造的车。
- 好主意。
IAN: What we'd like to do.
- Good idea.

815
00:40:54,460 --> 00:40:57,540
轮子画这么大，车身得做多大啊？
How big should it be with wheels that big?

816
00:40:57,580 --> 00:40:59,500
你们笑什么？
Why are you laughing?

817
00:41:01,660 --> 00:41:05,380
[观众议论纷纷]
- 这不是悍马！这是 E-Type！
[AUDIENCE MUTTER]
- It's not a Hummer! It's an E-Type.

818
00:41:05,420 --> 00:41:10,460
我画完了！绝了。
来看看你们画的。
I've finished! Fantastic.
Let's have a look at yours.

819
00:41:10,500 --> 00:41:12,180
发动机在哪儿？
- 在前面。
Where's the engine?
- In the front.

820
00:41:12,220 --> 00:41:13,900
前置发动机？
- 没错。
It's a front engine?
- Yes.

821
00:41:13,940 --> 00:41:16,140
啊，太棒了。
- 也可以后置。
Ah, that's fantastic.
- It could be rear.

822
00:41:16,180 --> 00:41:19,700
你这车头完全没有悬垂啊。
DB7 的悬垂可长得很。
You've got no overhang at all.
DB7's got quite a big one.

823
00:41:19,740 --> 00:41:22,180
一点悬垂都没有。
- 真是太漂亮了。
None at all.
- That's very beautiful.

824
00:41:22,220 --> 00:41:25,460
来看看这位前沃尔沃老兄
画成什么样了。
Let's have a look what
the former Volvo man's done.

825
00:41:26,900 --> 00:41:29,540
虽然还是草图，不过……
- 这简直一模一样！
Early days, but...
- It's exactly the same!

826
00:41:29,580 --> 00:41:32,540
[笑声]
- 你俩怎么做到的？
[LAUGHTER]
- How did you do that?

827
00:41:32,580 --> 00:41:35,380
简直一模一样！快看这个！
That's exactly the same! Look at that!

828
00:41:35,420 --> 00:41:36,940
简直就是同一个模子刻出来的。
That's exactly the same.

829
00:41:36,980 --> 00:41:40,020
能把这两张画拼在一起看看吗？
Can we get the two
of them brought together?

830
00:41:40,060 --> 00:41:43,260
我绝对支持你署名，他根本就是抄你的。
I'd definitely put your name
on it. He's nicked it.

831
00:41:43,300 --> 00:41:45,820
瞧瞧这个。
- 行。
Look at that.
- Okay.

832
00:41:47,380 --> 00:41:50,020
这俩画得完全一模一样！
They're exactly the same!

833
00:41:50,060 --> 00:41:51,740
彼得：要不然怎么叫我俩都给捷豹设计车呢。
PETER: Well, that's why
we're both designing Jaguars.

834
00:41:51,780 --> 00:41:54,420
看着这画，你们猜我想到什么了？
Do you know what I think looking at this?

835
00:41:54,460 --> 00:41:58,900
伙计们，我怀疑捷豹马上要推出
新一代 E-Type 了，
I suspect, boys, that there is
an E-Type Jag coming,

836
00:41:58,940 --> 00:42:02,460
而且你们俩心里早就一清二楚
它到底长什么样。
and that you both know
exactly what it looks like.

837
00:42:02,500 --> 00:42:06,740
如果你想为你心目中史上最美
的汽车投上一票，
If you want to vote for what
you think is the best-looking car ever,

838
00:42:06,780 --> 00:42:09,060
你可以去找个能连上因特网的地方，
you can do so by going near an internet,

839
00:42:09,100 --> 00:42:11,140
或者去邮筒投递一封信给我们，
or sending us a letter in a post-box,

840
00:42:11,180 --> 00:42:14,460
又或者用你的“蜂窝移动电话”
拨打电话参与。
or you can telephone
using a cellular telephone.

841
00:42:14,500 --> 00:42:17,380
不管怎样，非常感谢两位。
伊恩·卡勒姆和彼得·霍布里。
Anyway. Thank you very much.
Ian Callum and Peter Horbury.

842
00:42:17,420 --> 00:42:19,020
很高兴二位能赏光。
Lovely to have you along.

843
00:42:19,060 --> 00:42:20,620
谢谢。
Thank you.

844
00:42:25,740 --> 00:42:26,820
那么，
Well,

845
00:42:29,340 --> 00:42:31,740
录像带已经剪辑好了。
[嗤笑]
the tape has been edited.
[GIGGLES]

846
00:42:31,780 --> 00:42:33,980
噢，行行好，给我个痛快吧。
Oh, put me out of my misery, please.

847
00:42:34,020 --> 00:42:36,260
来看看圈速录像？
- 噢，放吧，求你了。
Shall we see the lap?
- Oh, go on, please.

848
00:42:36,300 --> 00:42:37,700
放录像。
Play the lap.

849
00:42:39,180 --> 00:42:40,540
噢！漂亮。
Oh! That's good.

850
00:42:43,460 --> 00:42:46,180
我可是在倾盆大雨里跑的。
I'm doing this in the pouring rain.

851
00:42:47,540 --> 00:42:50,820
[轮胎尖叫声]
- 跑得太烂了。
[TYRES SCREECH]
- That was rubbish.

852
00:42:50,860 --> 00:42:55,100
踩死，踩死，地板油，地板油，踩到底。二挡。
Floor, floor, floor, floor, floor. Second.

853
00:42:55,140 --> 00:42:58,220
噢！罗斯冲啊！
Ooh! Ross go!

854
00:42:58,260 --> 00:43:00,740
切弯切太狠了。
电视上看着明明慢多了！
That was too steep.
It looks slower on television!

855
00:43:02,700 --> 00:43:05,340
二挡。你刹车踩太早了...
Second. You broke too soon...

856
00:43:05,380 --> 00:43:08,260
进弯了，轻点刹车。
And you're in it, taps it.

857
00:43:08,300 --> 00:43:11,660
全油门，全油门。
Full power, full power.

858
00:43:11,700 --> 00:43:15,780
刹车。噢，你踩太早了！
Brake. Oh, you're too early!

859
00:43:15,820 --> 00:43:18,500
往里带。你得给点油门。
Bring it in. You've got to put
some power on.

860
00:43:18,540 --> 00:43:20,580
你动力全丢光了，老兄。
You lost all your power, son.

861
00:43:21,900 --> 00:43:24,460
最后一个弯搞砸了。
Messed up the last bend.

862
00:43:24,500 --> 00:43:26,940
你把最后一个弯给搞砸了。
- 可不是嘛。
You messed up the last bend.
- There you go.

863
00:43:26,980 --> 00:43:30,580
不过话说回来，正如你一开始说的，当时在下雨，没毛病。
Now, the thing is, as you pointed out
at the start, it was raining, OK.

864
00:43:30,620 --> 00:43:32,180
确实在下。
- 下雨会拖慢圈速。
It was.
- Rain slows you down.

865
00:43:32,220 --> 00:43:34,660
所以我们在想...在你跑完之后，
What we thought we'd do...
after you did that,

866
00:43:34,700 --> 00:43:38,460
我们把斯提格，
也就是我们驯养的赛车手派了出去。
we sent the Stig,
the tame racing driver out.

867
00:43:38,500 --> 00:43:42,100
他跑了一圈。干地圈速是1分46秒。
Now he went round. On a dry track, 1:46.

868
00:43:42,140 --> 00:43:46,460
我们又让他在湿地跑了一趟，
他跑出了1分50秒。
We sent him out in the wet
and he did a 1:50.

869
00:43:46,500 --> 00:43:49,580
换句话说，因为下雨，他慢了整整四秒。
So in other words, he was four seconds
slower because of the rain.

870
00:43:49,620 --> 00:43:52,540
你想知道你的湿地成绩是多少吗？
Would you like to know what
your wet time was?

871
00:43:52,580 --> 00:43:54,420
镜头拉近点，给罗斯一个大特写。
Camera in nice and tight, on Ross.

872
00:43:54,460 --> 00:43:56,300
我们告诉你...
- 我...
We tell you...
- I...

873
00:43:56,340 --> 00:43:58,580
我干嘛要来遭这份罪？
- 你觉得自己会比哈里·恩菲尔德更慢吗？
Why did I do this?
- Do you think it's slower than
Harry Enfield?

874
00:43:58,620 --> 00:44:01,020
我恨你！我真是恨死你了。
I hate you! I hate you so much.

875
00:44:01,060 --> 00:44:02,980
克拉克森，我迟早要找你算这笔账。
Clarkson, I am gonna get you
back at some point.

876
00:44:03,020 --> 00:44:05,620
记住，折算成干地成绩要扣掉四秒。
Remember, we take four seconds off
for a dry time.

877
00:44:05,660 --> 00:44:08,980
你的成绩是...罗斯·坎普。
- 这是湿地成绩。
Your time...Ross Kemp.
- This is the wet time.

878
00:44:09,020 --> 00:44:12,140
你在“廉价车大挑战”里的
湿地成绩...
Your wet time
Star-In-A-Reasonably-Priced-Car

879
00:44:12,180 --> 00:44:16,020
是1分54秒。
was one minute, 54 seconds.

880
00:44:16,060 --> 00:44:18,820
我觉得这成绩值得大家给点掌声。
I think a round of applause for that.

881
00:44:23,100 --> 00:44:26,540
哎呀，我还挺意外的。
- 因为说实话……
Well, I'm surprised.
- Because actually...

882
00:44:26,580 --> 00:44:30,980
我就把你贴这儿了。上面写了个“W”
代表是湿地成绩，行吧？
I'll put you there. I've got a "W" on it
for wet, OK?

883
00:44:31,020 --> 00:44:36,180
其实咱俩的成绩一模一样。
- 喜闻乐见。
Actually, you and I, we are the same.
- We like that.

884
00:44:36,220 --> 00:44:38,700
我很满意。
- 干得漂亮！女士们，
先生们，罗斯·坎普！
I like that.
- Well done. Ladies and
gentlemen, Ross Kemp.

885
00:44:38,740 --> 00:44:39,700
谢了，哥们儿。
Thanks, mate.

886
00:44:44,580 --> 00:44:48,780
好嘞，老奶奶玩定圆甩尾。
时刻到了。
Right. Grannies going doughnuts.
It is time.

887
00:44:48,820 --> 00:44:50,540
她们已经看过示范，知道该干什么了。
They've seen what they've got to do.

888
00:44:50,580 --> 00:44:52,500
现在唯一要做的就是亲自上阵试一把。
All they've got to do now is have a go.

889
00:44:52,540 --> 00:44:55,180
接下来就看战况如何了，所以
她们每人都要试一把。
And we get to see what happens, so
they're all gonna have a go.

890
00:44:55,220 --> 00:44:57,100
打头阵的是乔伊，先来露一手。
First up, Joy had a bash.

891
00:44:57,140 --> 00:45:00,260
乔伊今年73岁，不介意我报你的芳龄吧。
Joy is 73. You don't mind me saying that.

892
00:45:00,300 --> 00:45:04,260
来自伦敦，而且非常自豪地表示
她曾在一场征文比赛中获过奖。
From London. And is proud to say
she once won an essay-writing competition.

893
00:45:04,300 --> 00:45:07,180
那真是恭喜了，
不过今天这事可刺激得多。
So, congratulations to you
but this was a bit more exciting.

894
00:45:07,220 --> 00:45:08,700
来看看现场发生了什么。
Here's what happened.

895
00:45:08,740 --> 00:45:11,260
我够不着踏板。
- 我帮你把座椅往前调。
I can't reach the pedals.
- I'll put you forward.

896
00:45:12,700 --> 00:45:15,660
踩踩离合看，能踩到底吗？
Try the clutch. Can you get full travel?

897
00:45:15,700 --> 00:45:18,180
我开车从来没这么猛地抬过离合。
I never take my clutch off like that ever.

898
00:45:18,220 --> 00:45:21,540
我对待离合器向来都是小心翼翼的。
[引擎轰鸣]
I'm always very careful with my clutch.
[ENGINE REVS]

899
00:45:21,580 --> 00:45:23,740
要不……你知道的，轻点来？
Do it sort of, you know, gently?

900
00:45:23,780 --> 00:45:26,580
祝乔伊好运。
- 不过乔伊这会儿看着挺紧张的。
Good luck to Joy.
- She's quite nervous, is Joy though.

901
00:45:27,300 --> 00:45:30,260
[轮胎尖叫声]
[TYRES SCREECH]

902
00:45:31,020 --> 00:45:32,700
漂亮！
Yes!

903
00:45:32,740 --> 00:45:35,580
女：转起来转起来！
[笑声]
WOMAN: Get it going.
[LAUGHTER]

904
00:45:35,620 --> 00:45:38,740
踩下离合，拉高转速！
Dip the clutch now. Build the revs.

905
00:45:38,780 --> 00:45:40,340
把转速轰上去！猛抬离合！
Build the revs up. Let the clutch out hard.

906
00:45:40,380 --> 00:45:42,940
漂亮！稳住！
什么都别动！
That's it. Keep it there.
Don't do anything.

907
00:45:42,980 --> 00:45:44,740
就这么……
Just keep...

908
00:45:47,620 --> 00:45:50,780
别停！继续转！好样的！
Keep going! Keep going! Good girl.

909
00:45:50,820 --> 00:45:52,580
继续保持！
Keep going.

910
00:45:52,620 --> 00:45:55,780
冲冲冲！收点油！
油门别给那么大！对，就这样！
Go, go! Less throttle.
Not quite so much throttle. That's it!

911
00:45:55,820 --> 00:45:57,660
干得漂亮！
Well done.

912
00:45:57,700 --> 00:46:02,780
啊！我们……我们都看傻了。
Ah! We... we didn't know what to say.

913
00:46:02,820 --> 00:46:05,780
乔伊，这真是……太神了！
简直绝了！
Joy, that was... what a star!
That was fantastic!

914
00:46:05,820 --> 00:46:10,420
精彩还没完呢，懂了吧？
现在轮到另外三位大妈上场了。
That's not all, okay?
Now the next three have a go.

915
00:46:10,460 --> 00:46:13,820
哈蒙德：好嘞，这位是格温妮丝。
HAMMOND: Okay. This is Gwyneth.

916
00:46:13,860 --> 00:46:16,980
踩下离合。
拉高转速，弹离合！
Take the clutch.
Build the revs up. Clutch out.

917
00:46:17,020 --> 00:46:19,820
给油！多给点油！
很好，稳住别停！
Power! More power.
That's good. Keep it going.

918
00:46:19,860 --> 00:46:21,580
稳住别停！继续！
Keep it going. Keep going.

919
00:46:24,180 --> 00:46:25,500
女人们：耶——！
WOMEN: Yeeay!

920
00:46:25,540 --> 00:46:27,460
哇哦！冲进草地里了！
[吃吃笑]
Whoa! In the rough!
[GIGGLES]

921
00:46:30,460 --> 00:46:31,820
哈蒙德：现在轮到贝丽尔了。
HAMMOND: And now it's Beryl.

922
00:46:31,860 --> 00:46:33,020
这就对了。
That's better.

923
00:46:33,060 --> 00:46:34,860
把转速拉起来！
Build the revs up!

924
00:46:34,900 --> 00:46:37,260
油门踩到底，很好，保持住！
Keep your foot on
the floor, that's good, keep it going!

925
00:46:37,300 --> 00:46:40,180
油门别松！
很好，继续！
Keep going on the throttle!
That's good. Keep going.

926
00:46:40,220 --> 00:46:43,420
油门踩深点！
再狠一点，漂亮！稳住！
Harder on the throttle!
Harder, that's good! Keep it there!

927
00:46:43,460 --> 00:46:47,540
稳住别放！大脚油门踩死！
Keep it there! Hard on the throttle!

928
00:46:47,580 --> 00:46:49,220
哈蒙德：现在镜头给回格温妮丝。
HAMMOND: And back now to Gwyneth.

929
00:46:49,260 --> 00:46:52,780
继续，别停，稳住，
踩住别放！
Keep going, keep going, keep going,
keep going!

930
00:46:54,420 --> 00:46:57,580
[爆笑]
[HYSTERICAL LAUGHTER]

931
00:46:57,620 --> 00:47:01,460
漂亮。现在放开了甩，使劲！
哈蒙德：最后压轴的是安。
That's good. Let it out now, hard!
HAMMOND: And finally, Ann.

932
00:47:01,500 --> 00:47:04,540
保持住，就像刚才那样。
Keep it going, just the same.

933
00:47:04,580 --> 00:47:07,380
稳住，别停！
Keep it going, keep it going!

934
00:47:07,420 --> 00:47:09,740
你已经在转圈了！
干得漂亮。
[掌声]
You're going round and round!
Well done.
[APPLAUSE]

935
00:47:09,780 --> 00:47:11,620
听见掌声了吗？继续！
Can you hear the applause? Keep going.

936
00:47:11,660 --> 00:47:13,620
别停，你转得最棒了！
Don't stop, you're doing the best one!

937
00:47:13,660 --> 00:47:16,540
别停，继续转。
Don't stop. Keep it going.

938
00:47:16,580 --> 00:47:18,420
很好，继续。
That's good. Keep going.

939
00:47:19,460 --> 00:47:22,220
好，可以停了。直行开出来。
Okay, stop now. Go straight ahead.

940
00:47:22,260 --> 00:47:23,740
噢，太绝了！
Oh, fantastic!

941
00:47:23,780 --> 00:47:24,700
[欢呼]
[CHEERING]

942
00:47:24,740 --> 00:47:26,780
感觉怎么样？
- 爽翻了！
How was that?
- Brilliant!

943
00:47:26,820 --> 00:47:28,820
安：谢谢你。
ANN: Thank you.

944
00:47:28,860 --> 00:47:32,900
我简直无法形容现场有多刺激，
你们全都是大明星。
I can't tell you how exciting
that was to be there, you were all stars.

945
00:47:32,940 --> 00:47:36,260
不过这也证明了，你们懂的，
But we've proven then that, you know,

946
00:47:36,300 --> 00:47:38,300
老年人也是能把车开得飞起的。
older people can drive properly.

947
00:47:38,340 --> 00:47:41,660
但我们还想探探底，
这岁数极限到底能推到哪儿，
But we want to know
how far can you go with this,

948
00:47:41,700 --> 00:47:43,740
我是说，刚才那帮可都是七十几岁的。
I mean, you know, seventies.

949
00:47:43,780 --> 00:47:45,860
这位是萨迪。您好。
- 你好。
This is Sadie. Hello.
- Hello.

950
00:47:45,900 --> 00:47:48,780
萨迪，您多大年纪了？
- 我才不告诉你呢。
How old are you, Sadie?
- I'm not telling you.

951
00:47:48,820 --> 00:47:52,260
她八十了。
- 哪有！理查德！
She's 80.
- No! Richard!

952
00:47:52,300 --> 00:47:54,740
她真有八十岁。大家瞧好了。
She is 80. Watch this.

953
00:47:55,500 --> 00:47:58,700
[引擎轰鸣]
[ENGINE REVS]

954
00:47:58,740 --> 00:48:01,500
想象一下绕着皮卡迪利圆环这么漂！
Imagine doing that round Piccadilly Circus!

955
00:48:01,540 --> 00:48:04,380
[轮胎尖叫]
- 绝对能惊掉一堆人的下巴。哎哟我的天！
[TYRES SCREECH]
- You'd raise a few eyebrows. Ooh, my word!

956
00:48:04,420 --> 00:48:07,940
[老太太们七嘴八舌]
- 哎哟喂，来劲了！
